  <running_head>Castigatio Paral.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Cùm Ministri Gallicani, &amp; inter hos</l>
    <l n="2">doctissimus Molinæus, sæpiùs ad certa-</l>
    <l n="3">men provocarentur â Jesuitis, experti</l>
    <l n="4">sunt hi tantum nostrorum acumen, &amp;</l>
    <l n="5">in refutandis opinionibus pontificiis</l>
    <l n="6">tantam dexteritatem &amp; soliditatem, ut</l>
    <l n="7">cogitandū ipsis esset quâ aliâ viâ (quia</l>
    <l n="8">hac non succedebat) aggredi possent,</l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Cauterius</i> Jesuita pro sua subtilitate</l>
    <l n="10">suasit suis Pontificiis, ne in posterum</l>
    <l n="11">dogmata Romanæ ecclesiæ in disputa-</l>
    <l n="12">tionibus defenderent, viderent potiùs</l>
    <l n="13">quâ ratione nostros ad probanda fidei</l>
    <l n="14">nostræ dogmata ex puris scripturæ ver-</l>
    <l n="15">bis, adigere possent. Hoc stratagema,</l>
    <l n="16">tanquam omnium tutissimum Jesuit-</l>
    <l n="17">æ ambabus ulnis amplexi sunt, eaque uti</l>
    <l n="18">cœperunt in Gallia contra Molinæum</l>
    <l n="19">&amp; alios ecclesiæ ministros, quibus quæ-</l>
    <l n="20">stiones hinc inde anquisitas obiecerunt</l>
    <l n="21">ex scripturis demonstrandas. Huius</l>
    <l n="22">praxin suaserunt Jesuitæ Principi Vau-</l>
    <l n="23">dimontio contra Illust. Marchionem</l>
    <l n="24">Badensem. Eo etiam ufus est Harsche-</l>
    <l n="25">rus,</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Catchword/signature none visible. Some words in the scan are faint; "anquisitas" and "Harsche-rus" read with reasonable confidence.</notes>
</page>
